{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.SeparableInterfaceHypothesesHaveContentReal","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.SeparableInterfaceHypothesesHaveContentReal","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.SeparableInterfaceHypothesesHaveContent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.SeparableInterfaceContent.measured_asymmetry_attainable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.SeparableInterfaceContent.measured_asymmetry_attainable","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SeparableInterfaceHypothesesHaveContentReal.lean#L61-L69","doc":"**The measured asymmetry is attainable by a separable interface with distinct\nscalars.** This is the concrete form of `distinct_positive_scalars_reach_any_ratio`, and it\nis why the equal-scalars hypothesis is load-bearing rather than decorative: what it\nexcludes is not a small correction but the whole measured effect. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.SeparableInterfaceContent.measuredChannelAsymmetry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.SeparableInterfaceContent.measuredChannelAsymmetry","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SeparableInterfaceHypothesesHaveContentReal.lean#L55-L59","doc":"The two-nucleon channel asymmetry the corpus measures, `≈ 33.7055`\n(`computations/probes/two_nucleon_linking_matrix_channel_blind_probe.py`, which pins it to\nfour decimals). Carried as a numeral so the theorem below is falsifiable arithmetic rather\nthan a symbol. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.SeparableInterfaceContent.distinct_positive_scalars_reach_any_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.SeparableInterfaceContent.distinct_positive_scalars_reach_any_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SeparableInterfaceHypothesesHaveContentReal.lean#L42-L53","doc":"**The escape survives positivity.**\n\nOver `ℝ` with all four weights strictly positive — the physically admissible regime, since\nthe interface projector scalars satisfy `μ₊ + μ₋ = 1` with both positive for `q > 0`\n(`InterfaceScalar.proj_add_eq_one` and its ordering companions) — every positive ratio is\nstill attainable. So the release of the conclusion is not an artefact of admitting\nnegative or zero projector weights, which is the first objection it would meet. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.SeparableInterfaceContent.separability_hypotheses_have_content_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.SeparableInterfaceContent.separability_hypotheses_have_content_real","kind":"theorem","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SeparableInterfaceHypothesesHaveContentReal.lean#L27-L40","doc":"The generic content theorem specialised to the reals; the non-degeneracy hypothesis\n`(5 : ℝ) ≠ 6` is discharged by `norm_num`. Recorded so that the ring the corpus actually\nreasons over is on the record as an *instance* of the generic result, not a separate claim.\n\nWritten in the named-argument form `(R := ℝ)` that AGENTS.md §7c prescribes for the\narchimedean sibling. An earlier revision used `@f ℝ _` to dodge `check-sidecars.sh`,\nwhich counted the literal `(R :=` as evidence a file declares a *generic* result and so\nreported this correctly-split file as \"§7c MIXED\". That detector bug is fixed\n(`scripts/check-sidecars.sh`, fourth false-positive class), so the workaround is gone and\nthe prescribed spelling is back. ","signatureChunk":0}]}